<title>NETHERLANDS: KLENE 1996 NET PROFIT RISES 12 PCT.</title>
<headline>KLENE 1996 NET PROFIT RISES 12 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year 1996.</p>
<p>(in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net per shr (guilders)	     2.22 vs   1.96</p>
<p>    Net profit			     2.19 vs   1.96</p>
<p>    Dividend (guilders)		  0.90 vs   0.75</p>
<p>    Net sales			     60.04 vs  59.96</p>
<p>    Operating profit		     6.04 vs   5.22</p>
<p>    Interest charges		     0.54 vs   0.69</p>
<p>    Extraordinary gain		    nil vs   0.09</p>
<p>    Tax					1.94 vs   1.48</p>
<p>    Profit due to minorities	   1.37 vs   1.19</p>
<p>NOTES - Sweets maker Klene Holding NV said it had raised its</p>
<p>ownership of Klego Holding BV to 100 percent from 61.7 percent</p>
<p>in December and that profits due to minority interests in 1996</p>
<p>and previous years would in future flow to Klene Holding NV.</p>
<p>It said the guilder value of net sales was barely changed in</p>
<p>1996 with lower prices offsetting a 2.4 percent rise in volumes.</p>
<p>Klene said it expected improved sales and higher profits in</p>
<p>1997. It said shareholders had now approved a 10-for-one share</p>
<p>split announced on Jan 14 and which will take effect on Feb 7.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
